StarDist web application
Copyright 2026 Neurodesk contributors

src/stardist.js and src/stardist3d.js port, function by function, the 2D and 3D
post-processing of StarDist 0.9.1 (https://github.com/stardist/stardist:
_predict_sparse_generator, c_non_max_suppression_inds, polygons_to_label,
_COMMON_non_maximum_suppression_sparse, polyhedron_to_label) and the
normalization and tiling of CSBDeep 0.8.1 (https://github.com/CSBDeep/CSBDeep:
normalize, Tiling). Both are Copyright (c) 2018-2024, Uwe Schmidt, Martin
Weigert, under the BSD 3-Clause licence (LICENSE).

The models (stardist-2d-versatile-fluo.onnx, stardist-2d-versatile-he.onnx,
stardist-2d-paper-dsb2018.onnx and stardist-3d-demo.onnx) are StarDist's
pretrained models (https://github.com/stardist/stardist-models, release v0.1),
converted to ONNX by validation/convert_model.py. Copyright (c) 2018-2020,
Martin Weigert, Uwe Schmidt, under the BSD 3-Clause licence (LICENSE).

The H&E example (`skin-he-nuclei-2d.png`) is a 512 × 512 crop (`[200:712, 0:512]`)
of `skimage.data.skin()` (human epidermis and dermis with intradermal nevus,
Wikimedia Commons, author Kilbad, released to the public domain / CC0-1.0;
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Normal_Epidermis_and_Dermis_with_Intradermal_Nevus_10x.JPG).

The bundled clipper-lib 6.4.2 (https://sourceforge.net/projects/jsclipper/), a
JavaScript port of Angus Johnson's Clipper, is Copyright Angus Johnson 2010-2017
and is distributed under the Boost Software License 1.0, reproduced below. It
includes Tom Wu's BigInteger (jsbn), Copyright (c) 2005-2009 Tom Wu, under the
licence at http://www-cs-students.stanford.edu/~tjw/jsbn/LICENSE.

